00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.700
who represents Monterey Park in Alhambra.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.901
But first, my conversation

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:42.802
with Brandon Tsay.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:45.972
I spoke to him just before airtime

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:47.941
Brendan, first of all,

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.442
you've been through so much.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.411
How are you holding up

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:54.981
Well, I'm

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:55.915
doing way better

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:59.152
than I was at the night of the incident.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.487
So can you just take me through

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:03.490
what happened on Saturday night?

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:05.892
Okay.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.460
So Saturday night,

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.629
it was a Chinese New Year,

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.798
the Lunar New Year.

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:17.103
It was felt like a casual night.

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.739
Very typical.

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.040
We had our customers

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.108
coming in and out

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.911
for our social dance party.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:29.415
I was in the office

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.684
lobby most of the time.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.186
It was late into the evening

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:36.322
when the incident occurred.

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:40.793
When did you know to Sheppard sound

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.497
high?
When I knew something was happening.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.466
I heard the sound of the door

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:48.768
the front entrance shutting.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.737
And then there was a sound, a distinct

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:52.438
sound of metal

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.139
coming together

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:55.275
as if it was being rubbed together,

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:58.378
like someone was moving metal on metal

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.282
And how far away was

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:04.050
that sound from you?

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:09.489
It was no more than two meters away.

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:14.060
So did you see the person then?

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:15.628
No.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.430
What alerted me was a sound.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.333
I only turned after I heard that sound.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.068
What happened then?

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.838
After that,

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:29.809
I when I saw what I saw, I froze up.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:32.779
The man had a gun

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:34.814
The man was Brant and Brandy and a gun.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:37.784
He had a gun pointed at me.

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.319
It seemed like he was trying

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:42.422
to scout out the room for other people.

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:46.659
Was he saying anything?

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.194
I mean, you're saying he was

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:49.028
two meters away.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:49.829
So that's, what,

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:52.632
about six feet away from you?

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:53.800
He was pointing the gun at you

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:54.400
the whole time,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.736
or was he moving it around

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.306
It was in my general direction,

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:01.641
but when I saw him,

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:04.777
it was pointing straight at me, and

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:06.980
he was trying to look for other people.

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:09.916
Looking at the scouting room.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.051
And he didn't say anything at all.

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:17.056
He was silent, even stoic, very scary.

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.459
That he wasn't even saying anything

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:22.262
or giving me any instructions.

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:26.032
And so what happened

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:28.568
What happened

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:29.969
was it seemed like

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:32.538
he was preparing his weapon to fire,

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:34.340
changing

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.542
some sort of setting on the gun or

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:41.347
fixing his gun to prepare to fire.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.450
That's when I sprang into action.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.852
I realized

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:46.586
in the moment

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.421
that I needed to do something.

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.088
At this moment,

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:50.757
I need to grab the gun,

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:52.725
try to disarm him so

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:55.261
he couldn't do any harm to me or others.

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:59.065
So in that thought, I mean,

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:02.835
not a lot of people in this moment

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.704
would have maybe thought

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:07.707
to run away or to dove for cover.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:11.010
Your thought was to

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.578
get the gun

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:15.515
Oh, yes.

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:16.316
I'm not going to lie.

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:17.050
I did

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.819
freeze up when I saw him with the gun.

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:23.423
I had many thoughts where I would think

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:24.991
I'm going to die.

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:26.993
This is it.

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:29.228
This is the end for me.

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:31.230
But then something happened.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.365
You know, something came over me.

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:34.567
I just had this rush of thought

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.602
and adrenaline, you know,

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.272
in this sort of situation.

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.641
And I was able to come to a conclusion

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:43.076
that I needed to do something.

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:45.812
I needed to grab the gun and saved myself

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:47.013
and the people inside.

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.915
And you're talking about

00:05:48.915 --> 00:05:50.316
all these thoughts you had.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.318
I assume this is all happening

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:54.420
within split seconds in your head.

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:57.290
How long were you standing there

00:05:57.457 --> 00:06:00.193
looking at him, seeing the gun before you

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.327
you acted

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.732
No more than 2 seconds.

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:07.834
No more than 2 seconds.

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:10.570
I saw a window of opportunity

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:13.306
that he was distracted with his gun

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.141
and took it.

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:16.609
I took him to action

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:18.344
once I saw the opportunity.

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:21.280
So what exactly did you do

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:26.085
I made sure that nothing

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:28.488
was in my way to

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:30.123
attack him.

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:33.760
And lunged at him with both my arms

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:37.497
and grabbed his weapon with both my arms.

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:39.732
And were you immediately able

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:42.535
to take it out of his grasp?

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:46.773
know, there's a big struggle, actually.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.676
The struggle went on into the lobby

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:54.614
He hit me several times

00:06:54.614 --> 00:06:56.649
in the face behind my head.

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:57.417
With what?

00:06:57.417 --> 00:06:58.551
With his hand back.

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:01.154
He was with his hands.

00:07:01.154 --> 00:07:02.822
He was trying to feed me away

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:04.290
from his gun

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.092
while trying to gain

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:08.194
control of his weapon.

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:09.295
But at the same time,

00:07:09.295 --> 00:07:12.465
I was trying to divert the weapon away

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:13.065
from me,

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:14.467
away from the ballroom

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:16.102
and down on the ground

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:17.236
in case he did fire

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:19.439
and that

00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:22.008
I was also trying to free from his grass

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:24.143
and using my elbows, using my shoulders,

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.812
trying to use my body way

00:07:25.812 --> 00:07:28.581
to free the weapon away from him.

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:33.486
And how long was this struggle for

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:35.588
I would say

00:07:35.588 --> 00:07:37.490
the struggle lasted

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:41.160
40 seconds, but it felt like way longer,

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.396
felt like an eternity with the adrenaline

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:45.631
and my thoughts.

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:47.467
I was always thinking about

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:48.701
if I let go of this gun,

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:51.204
what would happen to me?

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:51.971
The people around me,

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:54.841
my friends, my family, how would they

00:07:55.575 --> 00:07:56.342
be affected

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:58.044
if I let this dangerous

00:07:58.044 --> 00:08:00.279
individual run around and work?

00:08:00.546 --> 00:08:02.215
Were you saying anything to him

00:08:02.215 --> 00:08:03.015
during the struggle?

00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:05.718
Was he saying anything to you?

00:08:07.753 --> 00:08:08.154
No.

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:10.790
We had no verbal

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:11.324
threat.

00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:13.826
We had no verbal conversation.

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:15.728
But he seemed like he didn't

00:08:15.728 --> 00:08:17.530
want to talk from the start.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:18.030
It seemed like

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:21.300
he was trying to take action instead of

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:23.035
have any type of

00:08:23.035 --> 00:08:24.770
conversation or commands.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:25.304
So you said it

00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:27.473
went on for 40 or so seconds.

00:08:27.473 --> 00:08:28.107
And then what?

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:28.808
Then what happened?

00:08:28.808 --> 00:08:30.443
How did you finally get it away?

00:08:34.347 --> 00:08:35.248
Well,

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:36.182
as he was trying

00:08:36.182 --> 00:08:38.818
to attack me with his arm and his hands,

00:08:39.285 --> 00:08:41.721
I used the opportunity to

00:08:43.923 --> 00:08:46.893
yank the gun away on his office

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:48.060
opposite side

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:50.563
so he wasn't able to fully

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:52.732
use his strength

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:55.401
to keep the gun in position.

00:08:56.102 --> 00:08:58.771
And that's when I was able to

00:08:58.771 --> 00:09:01.240
pull the gun away from him and

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.141
create some distance

00:09:02.141 --> 00:09:03.876
between him and the gun

00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:06.045
I had.

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:08.314
Have you ever had you ever held that?

00:09:08.314 --> 00:09:09.115
Go ahead.

00:09:11.851 --> 00:09:13.953
No, I have never held a gun before.

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:17.790
It's scary to even the weight of the gun.

00:09:18.291 --> 00:09:20.893
It's haunted on me how this object was

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.061
something that could end

00:09:22.061 --> 00:09:23.696
in a person's life.

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:26.699
So you have the gun and you

00:09:26.699 --> 00:09:28.167
create some distance.

00:09:28.167 --> 00:09:30.436
Did he did he run away then?

00:09:33.172 --> 00:09:34.073
No.

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:34.840
At this point,

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:35.641
he looked like

00:09:35.641 --> 00:09:37.410
he was still trying to fight.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:39.412
But I pointed the gun at him

00:09:40.012 --> 00:09:42.949
and told him, go go away.

00:09:42.982 --> 00:09:45.084
You got to leave. Go get out here.

00:09:46.452 --> 00:09:47.520
And I also threatened him

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.388
that I would shoot.

00:09:49.388 --> 00:09:50.523
And

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.224
I had many thoughts

00:09:52.224 --> 00:09:53.159
I thought I would

00:09:53.159 --> 00:09:54.160
actually have to kill him

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.729
as actually shoot a person.

00:09:56.729 --> 00:09:59.832
Were you prepared to do that?

00:10:01.534 --> 00:10:03.636
Yes, I was prepared to fire,

00:10:03.636 --> 00:10:06.272
but I didn't want to shoot him anywhere.

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:07.106
That would be fatal.

00:10:07.106 --> 00:10:08.774
I wanted to see if I could

00:10:08.774 --> 00:10:11.644
aim at the legs or the arms, you know,

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:13.713
something that would stop him from

00:10:13.713 --> 00:10:15.147
trying to cover the gun.

